Day 1: Introduction to the Opium Wars (45 minutes)

1.   Begin the lesson by introducing the topic of the Opium Wars and asking students if they have any prior knowledge about the topic.
2.   Provide students with a brief overview of the Opium Wars and their causes and effects.
3.   Distribute handouts with information about the Opium Wars and have students work in small groups to discuss the causes and effects of the wars.
4.   Have students share their findings with the class.
5.   Use a whiteboard to create a timeline of the Opium Wars and have students add the causes and effects to the timeline.
6.   Have students discuss the role of opium in the history of China and Britain.
7.   Have students work in small groups to create a short skit that explores the causes and effects of the Opium Wars.

Day 2: Drama Techniques (45 minutes)

1.   Begin the lesson by reviewing the causes and effects of the Opium Wars and the role of opium in the history of China and Britain.
2.   Introduce the students to the concept of drama techniques and how they can be used to explore complex issues.
3.   Have students work in small groups to create a short skit that explores the causes and effects of the Opium Wars using drama techniques.
4.   Have students perform their skits for the class and discuss the effectiveness of the techniques used.
